keep HEIF and HEVC on with 10-bit color, and put them back after

Settings > Formats (classes7 com/oplus/camera/setting/h2 s(), onPreferenceChange) now calls mm/DV formats(), which
runs after the stock handler and then sets the three switches from the stored values:
- "10-bit color" on: the HEIF (n9.d B0/C0) and HEVC (n9.d z0, n9.f p) values are saved in
  pref_10bit_photo_codec_before / pref_10bit_video_codec_before, then both are set on.
- "10-bit color" off: both go back to the saved values.
- HEIF off while 10-bit is on: 10-bit goes off, HEVC goes back to its saved value.
- HEVC off while 10-bit is on: 10-bit goes off, HEIF goes back to its saved value.
mm/DV resume() (camera onResume) applies the same rule to an existing 10-bit-on state. With 10-bit on, C0 (the
codec the mode-start rewrite in com/oplus/camera/nb restores outside 10-bit modes) is HEIF, so Settings no longer
shows HEIF off after a visit to Video. With 10-bit off both are plain 8-bit (IMG20261021213131.heic: hevc Main
yuv420p tiles; VID20261021213127.mp4: hevc Main yuv420p). Source: .claude/tools/cam7/dolby/mm/DV.java.

